/**
\page MITKCmdAppsPage MITK Command-Line Apps

\tableofcontents

\section MITKCmdAppsPageIntro What are command-line apps?

MITK command-line apps are small executables that each perform one processing
task without a graphical user interface: converting files, fusing 3D images
into a dynamic image, rasterizing contours, registering and mapping images,
fitting models to time series, computing SUV images, and more. They are built
on the same MITK modules as the MITK Workbench, so they read and write the same
file formats and produce the same results as the corresponding Workbench
plugins.

Use them to process many datasets in a script, to integrate MITK functionality
into a pipeline, or to run MITK on a machine without a display.

\section MITKCmdAppsPageWhere Where to find them

\subsection MITKCmdAppsPageWhereInstaller In the MITK Workbench installer

The apps marked "Workbench installer" in the tables below are part of the
official MITK Workbench release for Windows and Linux. After installation you
find

<ul>
<li> the executables in the <tt>bin/</tt> directory next to
<tt>MitkWorkbench</tt>, and
<li> a launcher script per app in the <tt>apps/</tt> directory
(<tt>apps/MitkFileConverter.bat</tt> on Windows,
<tt>apps/MitkFileConverter.sh</tt> on Linux).
</ul>

Use the launcher scripts. They set up the library search path and forward all
arguments to the executable, so you can call them from any working directory:

\code
C:\Program Files\MITK 2026.06\apps\MitkFileConverter.bat -i image.dcm -o image.nrrd
~/MITK-2026.06/apps/MitkFileConverter.sh -i image.dcm -o image.nrrd
\endcode

On macOS the executables are located inside the application bundle at
<tt>MitkWorkbench.app/Contents/MacOS/</tt> and can be started from there
directly.

\subsection MITKCmdAppsPageWhereBuild In a build tree

In your own build of MITK the executables are located in the <tt>bin/</tt>
directory of the MITK build tree (on Windows in <tt>bin/Release/</tt> or
<tt>bin/Debug/</tt>). On Windows use the generated batch files
<tt>bin/Mitk&lt;App&gt;_release.bat</tt> and <tt>bin/Mitk&lt;App&gt;_debug.bat</tt>,
which set up the PATH and forward all arguments.

Which apps are built is controlled per module by a CMake option named
<tt>BUILD_&lt;Module&gt;CmdApps</tt> (see the tables below). The build
configuration <tt>WorkbenchRelease</tt> enables the apps that ship in the
installer, <tt>MITK_BUILD_ALL_APPS</tt> enables all of them, and the build
configuration <tt>CoreCmdApps</tt> builds only the file conversion apps without
Qt for headless machines. See \ref BuildInstructionsPage for building MITK.

\section MITKCmdAppsPageConventions Common conventions

All apps share the same command-line syntax, provided by the class
mitkCommandLineParser.

<ul>
<li> Every argument has a long name with two dashes and a short name with one
dash, for example <tt>--input</tt> and <tt>-i</tt>. Values follow the argument
separated by a space: <tt>-i image.nrrd</tt>. List arguments take several
values: <tt>-i a.nrrd b.nrrd c.nrrd</tt>.
<li> <tt>--help</tt> (<tt>-h</tt>) prints a description of all arguments and
exits with code 0. The help text is also printed when a required argument is
missing; the app then exits with code 1.
<li> <tt>--version</tt> prints the Git commit and branch the app was built from
and exits with code 0.
<li> <tt>--xml</tt> prints a machine-readable description of the app and its
arguments in the format of the Slicer execution model and exits with code 0.
This is meant for tools that generate user interfaces or pipeline nodes from
it; nothing else is printed in this case.
<li> Otherwise the first line of output is <tt>Running Command Line Utility ...</tt>
with the app title and the MITK version.
<li> Apps return exit code 0 on success and 1 on failure unless their page
documents other codes. Some apps also return 0 when they cannot load the input
and stop early; the individual pages say so.
</ul>

Input and output files can be any format MITK reads or writes, for example
NRRD, NIfTI, MetaImage, or DICOM. A directory of DICOM files can be passed as
input wherever an image is expected. Multi-label segmentations are read and
written in MITK's NRRD based segmentation format or as DICOM SEG.

\subsection MITKCmdAppsPageConventionsJson Passing JSON option strings

Some apps take JSON dictionaries as argument values, for example
<tt>--input-options</tt> of MitkFileConverter or <tt>--parameters</tt> of
MitkMatchImage. The quoting depends on the shell:

<ul>
<li> bash, zsh and other Unix shells: enclose the JSON in single quotes.
\code
MitkFileConverter -i seg.nrrd -o seg.nii.gz --output-options '{"Save strategy": "instance"}'
\endcode
<li> Windows Command Prompt (cmd.exe): enclose the JSON in double quotes and
double every inner double quote.
\code
MitkFileConverter -i seg.nrrd -o seg.nii.gz --output-options "{""Save strategy"": ""instance""}"
\endcode
<li> PowerShell 7.3 and newer: single quotes work as in bash. Older PowerShell
versions pass the argument through the Windows command line, so the inner
double quotes have to be escaped with a backslash.
\code
MitkFileConverter -i seg.nrrd -o seg.nii.gz --output-options '{\"Save strategy\": \"instance\"}'
\endcode
</ul>

\section MITKCmdAppsPageList List of command-line apps

The "Availability" column tells whether an app is part of the MITK Workbench
installer or which CMake option builds it.

\subsection MITKCmdAppsPageListCore File conversion and image handling

| App | Purpose | Availability |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \subpage MITKFileConverterPage "MitkFileConverter" | Converts between all file formats MITK can read and write, with control over readers, writers and their options. | Workbench installer |
| \subpage MitkImageTypeConverterPage "MitkImageTypeConverter" | Converts the pixel type of an image, e.g. to float or unsigned short. | Workbench installer |
| \subpage MitkFuse3Dto4DImagePage "MitkFuse3Dto4DImage" | Fuses several 3D images with the same geometry into one dynamic (3D+t) image. | Workbench installer |
| \subpage MitkSplit4Dto3DImagePage "MitkSplit4Dto3DImages" | Splits a dynamic (3D+t) image into one 3D image per time step. | Workbench installer |

\subsection MITKCmdAppsPageListSegmentation Segmentation

| App | Purpose | Availability |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \subpage MitkConvertToMultiLabelSegmentationPage "MitkConvertToMultiLabelSegmentation" | Merges images, surfaces and contours into one multi-label segmentation. | Workbench installer |
| \subpage MitkContoursToImagePage "MitkContoursToImage" | Rasterizes contours (e.g. DICOM RTSTRUCT) into binary masks or segmentations. | Workbench installer |

\subsection MITKCmdAppsPageListDICOM DICOM

| App | Purpose | Availability |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \subpage MitkDICOMVolumeDiagnosticsPage "MitkDICOMVolumeDiagnostics" | Reports how MITK would group a set of DICOM files into volumes and why volumes are split. | Workbench installer |

\subsection MITKCmdAppsPageListRegistration Registration

| App | Purpose | Availability |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \subpage MitkMatchImagePage "MitkMatchImage" | Registers a moving image to a target image with a MatchPoint algorithm and stores the registration. | Workbench installer |
| \subpage MitkMapImagePage "MitkMapImage" | Maps an image or segmentation into a target geometry using a registration. | Workbench installer |
| \subpage MitkStitch3DImagesPage "MitkStitchImages" | Maps and stitches several 3D images into one image with a common geometry. | Workbench installer |

\subsection MITKCmdAppsPageListModelFit Dynamic data and model fitting

| App | Purpose | Availability |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \subpage MitkGenericFittingPage "MitkGenericFitting" | Fits a linear or user-defined model to the time curve of every voxel of a dynamic image. | Workbench installer |
| \subpage MitkPixelDumpPage "MitkPixelDump" | Writes the voxel values of one or more images, optionally within a mask, into a CSV file. | Workbench installer |

\subsection MITKCmdAppsPageListPerfusion Perfusion (pharmacokinetics)

| App | Purpose | Availability |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \subpage MitkMRSignal2ConcentrationPage "MitkMRSignal2Concentration" | Converts dynamic T1 or T2 weighted MR signal images into contrast agent concentration images. | <tt>BUILD_PerfusionCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkMRPerfusionPage "MitkMRPerfusion" | Fits pharmacokinetic models (e.g. Tofts) to dynamic contrast enhanced MR data and writes parameter maps. | <tt>BUILD_PerfusionCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkCurveDescriptorPage "MitkCurveDescriptor" | Computes descriptive parameters (e.g. area under the curve, time to peak) of the time curves of a dynamic image. | <tt>BUILD_PerfusionCmdApps</tt> |

\subsection MITKCmdAppsPageListPET PET

| App | Purpose | Availability |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \subpage MitkPETSUVCalculationPage "MitkPETSUVCalculation" | Converts a PET activity image into a standardized uptake value (SUV) image. | Workbench installer |

\subsection MITKCmdAppsPageListBasic Basic image processing

| App | Purpose | Availability |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \subpage MitkSingleImageArithmeticPage "MitkSingleImageArithmetic" | Applies unary functions (sqrt, log10, sin, ...) to every voxel of an image. | <tt>BUILD_BasicImageProcessingCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkTwoImageArithmeticPage "MitkTwoImageArithmetic" | Adds, subtracts, multiplies or divides two images voxel by voxel. | <tt>BUILD_BasicImageProcessingCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkImageAndValueArithmeticPage "MitkImageAndValueArithmetic" | Adds, subtracts, multiplies or divides an image and a constant value. | <tt>BUILD_BasicImageProcessingCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkMaskRangeBasedFilteringPage "MitkMaskRangeBasedFiltering" | Removes mask voxels whose image intensity is outside a given range. | <tt>BUILD_BasicImageProcessingCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkMaskOutlierFilteringPage "MitkMaskOutlierFiltering" | Removes mask voxels whose image intensity is a statistical outlier (3 sigma). | <tt>BUILD_BasicImageProcessingCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkResampleImagePage "MitkResampleImage" | Resamples an image to a new voxel spacing. | <tt>BUILD_BasicImageProcessingCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkResampleMaskPage "MitkResampleMask" | Resamples a binary mask to a new voxel spacing while keeping it binary. | <tt>BUILD_BasicImageProcessingCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkLaplacianOfGaussianPage "MitkLaplacianOfGaussian" | Computes the Laplacian of Gaussian of an image at a given scale. | <tt>BUILD_BasicImageProcessingCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkMultiResolutionPyramidPage "MitkMultiResolutionPyramid" | Computes a Gaussian multi-resolution pyramid, one image per level. | <tt>BUILD_BasicImageProcessingCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkForwardWaveletPage "MitkForwardWavelet" | Computes an isotropic wavelet decomposition, one image per sub-band. | <tt>BUILD_BasicImageProcessingCmdApps</tt> |

\subsection MITKCmdAppsPageListClassification Radiomics and classification

| App | Purpose | Availability |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \subpage MitkCLGlobalImageFeaturesPage "MitkCLGlobalImageFeatures" | Computes radiomics features (first order, texture, shape, ...) of an image within a mask. | <tt>BUILD_ClassificationCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkCLMRNormalizationPage "MitkCLMRNormalization" | Normalizes MR intensities with respect to a reference region. | <tt>BUILD_ClassificationCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkCLN4Page "MitkCLN4" | Corrects MR bias fields with the N4 algorithm. | <tt>BUILD_ClassificationCmdApps</tt> |
| \subpage MitkCLScreenshotPage "MitkCLScreenshot" | Renders screenshots of an image with overlaid segmentations. | <tt>BUILD_ClassificationCmdApps</tt> |

